        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is well-placed in most respects: `IdentityKeyUtils` follows the existing `E164PhoneNumbers` static-utility convention in the `util` package, its javadoc correctly justifies why the helpers live outside the MapStruct mapper (matching the established note in `OwnerMapper.regionOf`), and `toIdentityKey` remains the single source of truth reused by both the DTO and the 409 check. But there is one concrete structural problem.\n\n**Finding: `IdentityKeyUtils.sha256Hex` is a third copy of the SHA-256-to-hex routine.**\n\nThe new `sha256Hex` (lines 90\u2013107 of `IdentityKeyUtils.java`) duplicates a digest-to-hex loop that already exists twice:\n\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.sha256UpperHex` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:350`) \u2014 identical `MessageDigest.getInstance(\"SHA-256\")` \u2192 `StringBuilder` \u2192 `String.format(\"%02X\"/\"%02x\")` \u2192 `IllegalStateException(\"SHA-256 not available\")` structure, differing only in hex case.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.householdIdFor` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:302`) \u2014 the same loop, truncated to 12 chars.\n\nThe change introduces a dedicated hashing helper in the `util` package \u2014 which is exactly the natural home to consolidate these \u2014 yet leaves the two existing copies in place and adds a third. A maintainer would expect the new util to become the single hashing helper (e.g. a shared `sha256Hex` plus an upper-case/truncating variant, or a case parameter) with the controller and service delegating to it, rather than three near-identical private implementations of the same primitive spread across three layers.\n\nActionable: put the SHA-256 hex logic in one place (the new util) and have `OwnerRestControllerV1.sha256UpperHex` and `ClinicServiceImpl.householdIdFor` call through to it, so the digest-to-hex code exists once.\n\nMinor (optional): in `findPossibleDuplicate`, `soundex(existing.getLastName())` is recomputed per existing owner even though `toIdentityKey(existing)` already computes the same soundex internally \u2014 the two soundex computations per candidate are inherent to hashing the key, but worth a note if a cheaper pre-filter is wanted later. Not blocking."
